outcome of the measurement has to be this value, call it ff.  Even if
we repeat the measurement many times we always have to obtain ff.
Suppose now that someone just prior to our measurement performs a
strong measurement searching for the particle at a distance l far
outside the well.  There is an exponentially small but non-zero
probability that he will find the particle there:

